    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0786" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/303B.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Messrs. Kuhn, Loeb &amp; Co</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: In confirmation of the Department’s
                    telegram to you of this date,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d845-f1"/> I will say that a
                        letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d845-f2"/> has been received from Dr. Roland P.
                    Falkner, Financial Representative of Liberia, inclosing copies of the revises of
                    the several Liberian loan agreements, dated February 23, 1912. Dr. Falkner also
                    incloses copy of his letter to you<anchor n="1" xml:id="d845-f3"/> confirming
                    the last amendments to the contracts.</p>
                <p>The Department has examined the agreements as now amended in accordance with
                    suggestions made by you and by Dr. Falkner. In their present form they appear to
                    be satisfactory to the Department. We shall depend upon you to communicate them
                    to the Governments concerned through the other bankers, and also to send us
                    copies to give, as a matter of courtesy, to the French, German and British
                    Embassies here.</p>
                <p>It is hoped that it may be your pleasure to have Dr. Falkner come to New York
                    City at an early date in order that the agreements may be signed.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
